 CSS BACKGROUND-REPEAT 


BACKGROUND-REPEAT
=================
background-repeat controls
how a background image repeats
inside an element.

By default,
background images repeat
both horizontally and vertically.


DEFAULT BEHAVIOR
================
If background-repeat is not written,
the image will repeat automatically.

background-repeat: repeat;


NO REPEAT
=========
The image appears only once.

.box {
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
}


REPEAT HORIZONTALLY
==================
The image repeats only from
left to right.

.box {
    background-repeat: repeat-x;
}


REPEAT VERTICALLY
================
The image repeats only from
top to bottom.

.box {
    background-repeat: repeat-y;
}


MULTIPLE BACKGROUND IMAGES
=========================
Each image can have
its own repeat value.

.layered {
    background-repeat: no-repeat, repeat;
}


COMMON MISTAKES
===============
- Forgetting background-repeat
- Expecting image to stop repeating by default
- Using large images that do not need repeat


PRACTICE
========
Add a small image as background.
Try each repeat value one by one
and observe the difference.

.box {
    height: 200px;
    background-image: url("images/pattern.png");
    background-repeat: repeat;
}
